From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:19:38 -0700
Subject: Set XMLParsingRust to experimental and fix XMLDocumentParserRs bugs

This CL enables XMLParsingRust as an experimental runtime feature and
fixes several bugs in XMLDocumentParserRs uncovered by the test suite:

- In XMLDocumentParserRs::StartElementNs, check IsStopped() after
CreateElement and set attributes individually when a custom element
constructor has run, matching XMLDocumentParser::StartElementNs. This
copies https://crrev.com/c/8501725 for the non-rust parser.

- Guard XMLDocumentParserRs::ProcessEvents against re-entrant Append()
and Finish() calls during synchronous inline script execution by
buffering incoming chunks in pending_src_ and deferring Finish(). This
copies https://crrev.com/c/8419603 for the non-rust parser.

- Ignore ImmutableEntitiesError::StandaloneDocument in
add_xhtml_entities instead of panicking when an XHTML doctype is used
with standalone="yes".

- Use XMLDocumentParserRs in DOMPatchSupport::PatchDocument when Rust
XML parsing is enabled, and include saw_error_ in
XMLDocumentParserRs::WellFormed().

- Avoid setting saw_xsl_transform_ or entering XML viewer mode on
documents that have already been transformed by XSLT.

- Record script_start_position_ at the token following the opening

Bug: 435623334
Fixed: 569659189
Change-Id: Id8fcad269a4b0e0a3fa91930570ca1c9eacbe311
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8602619
Auto-Submit: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: David Baron <dbaron@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726224}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Carried: the in_process_events_ re-entrancy guard and pending_src_ buffering
in Append()/ProcessEvents(), finish_called_ handling moved into EndInternal(),
UpdateScriptStartPositionIfNeeded(), the IsStopped() check after
CreateElement(), per-attribute setAttribute() after a synchronous custom
element constructor, WellFormed() including saw_error_, the
ImmutableEntitiesError handling in xml_ffi.rs and the DOMPatchSupport parser
selection. Not carried: the XSLT / CAP-alert handling (saw_xsl_transform_,
IsXSLTAllowed(), original_source_for_transform_) and
XMLParserReplaceLoneSurrogates, which do not exist on this branch, and the
XMLParsingRust status change (the feature stays disabled as on this branch).
Web test expectation changes were not carried.

